    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hipatterns\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen I open a large file with a large number of highlight/syntax groups, the error is thrown continuously.\n\n```\n   Error  09:45:53 msg_show.emsg E849: Too many highlight and syntax groups\n   Error  09:45:53 msg_show.lua_error Error executing vim.schedule lua callback: .../local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:648: Invalid highlight name: 'MiniHipatterns_f5deae_bg'\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_set_hl'\n\t.../local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:648: in function 'group'\n\t.../local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:947: in function ''\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n   Error  09:45:53 msg_show.emsg E849: Too many highlight and syntax groups\n   Error  09:45:53 msg_show.lua_error Error executing vim.schedule lua callback: .../local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:648: Invalid highlight name: 'MiniHipatterns_e2efdd_bg'\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_set_hl'\n\t.../local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:648: in function 'group'\n\t.../local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:947: in function ''\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n```\n\nA sample file: https://github.com/meodai/color-names/blob/HEAD/src/colornames.csv\n\nIs there anyway I can prevent this error? Can the highlight be rendered as I scroll limiting the number of highlight/syntax groups when opening a big file of hex colors.\n\nOnce the error happens, I cannot use any of my snacks.nvim modules (possibly other side-effects as well).\n\n```\nE5108: Error executing lua: .../nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/core/picker.lua:206: attempt to index field 'layout' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n\t.../nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/core/picker.lua:206: in function 'on_current_tab'\n\t.../nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/core/picker.lua:66: in function 'get'\n\t...l/share/nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/init.lua:77: in function 'files'\n\t/home/maurice/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/snacks.lua:447: in function </home/maurice/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/snacks.lua:447>\nE5108: Error executing lua: .../nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/core/picker.lua:206: attempt to index field 'layout' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n\t.../nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/core/picker.lua:206: in function 'on_current_tab'\n\t.../nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/core/picker.lua:66: in function 'get'\n\t...l/share/nvim/lazy/snacks.nvim/lua/snacks/picker/init.lua:77: in function 'grep'\n\t/home/maurice/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/snacks.lua:424: in function </home/maurice/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/snacks.lua:424>\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\nDefault example usage\n\n```\nlocal hipatterns = require('mini.hipatterns')\nhipatterns.setup({\n  highlighters = {\n    -- Highlight standalone 'FIXME', 'HACK', 'TODO', 'NOTE'\n    fixme = { pattern = '%f[%w]()FIXME()%f[%W]', group = 'MiniHipatternsFixme' },\n    hack  = { pattern = '%f[%w]()HACK()%f[%W]',  group = 'MiniHipatternsHack'  },\n    todo  = { pattern = '%f[%w]()TODO()%f[%W]',  group = 'MiniHipatternsTodo'  },\n    note  = { pattern = '%f[%w]()NOTE()%f[%W]',  group = 'MiniHipatternsNote'  },\n\n    -- Highlight hex color strings (`#rrggbb`) using that color\n    hex_color = hipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color(),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOpen the sample file: https://github.com/meodai/color-names/blob/HEAD/src/colornames.csv\n\nOnce the error happens, one of the side effect of the error is unable to run snacks.nvim functions. Example:\n```\n:lua Snacks.picker.files()\n```",
