        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello @mau-mauricelim,\n\nAccording to `:h E849`:\n\n> The maximum number of syntax groups is 19999.\n\nYour file contains 31899 lines, where each line has a unique color code resulting in a group.\nAs such, I don't think this is a bug.\nI can also reproduce with for example the uga-rosa/ccc.nvim plugin.\n\n> Is there anyway I can prevent this error? Can the highlight be rendered as I scroll limiting the number of highlight/syntax groups when opening a big file of hex colors.\n\nLimiting the number of groups during scrolling is not supported. My first guess is that it is not trivial to implement.\n\nYou could split the file in two halves to avoid the error. Both halves correctly display the highlighting.\n\nIt is also possible to conditionally disable the plugin, for example based on file size.\nAdd `after/ftplugin/csv.lua` to your config. Example content:\n\n```lua\nlocal function get_buf_size()\n  local bufnr = vim.api.nvim_get_current_buf()\n  local ok, stats = pcall(function() return vim.uv.fs_stat(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(bufnr)) end)\n  if not (ok and stats) then return end\n  return stats.size\nend\n\nlocal size = get_buf_size()\nif not size or size < 380000 then return end\n\n-- File -probably- contains too much unique color codes...\nvim.b.minihipatterns_disable = true\n```",
