        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Hi @abeldekat, thank you for your suggestion. I'll probably add this in temporarily as a quick fix. But I do think that this is not a reliable solution as I may have a large file with only a few highlights and I want it to be active. It would be good if I can somehow detect if there are a large numbers of highlights and disable the highlighting. But I know this may be a non-trivial task.\n\nYes, it was intended as a quick fix. Perhaps that can be improved a bit, depending on your workflow.\nA file with 30000+ hex colors seems to be intended as a catalogue. If you know this beforehand, you could name the file in some special way, in order to disable mini.hipatterns based on that name in `after/ftplugin/csv.lua`",
            "created_at": "2026-04-10T14:33:37Z",
