        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be (somewhat) resolved on the latest `main` by limiting a total number of different highlight groups the `gen_highlighter.hex_color()` is allowed to created. Can be controlled by [`opts.max_number`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/418ef4930ddabe80f449c6f1323f8b6abb172d1c/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L444) (the name chosen to be consistent with what 'mini.files' uses). So opening a file with a lot of hex colors will now not error, *but* it will also not show all colors (but only `opts.max_number` first of them).\n\nAlthough after neovim/neovim#39133 using `pcall()` for hiding the error message should be possible in at least Neovim 0.13 (probably in 0.12.2), reaching that limit is bad in itself. So I did follow the [@abeldekat idea](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2360#issuecomment-4224555805) both in 'mini.hipatterns' and in upstream Neovim's `vim.lsp.document_color`.",
